{
  "about": "Agent conformance falsifiers. Paths are relative to lab/agent-conformance. Replace each old text exactly once; every named test must run and fail, then pass after restoring the original bytes. command: lab is reserved for the provider-owned shared runner; run these by hand until that arm exists. Run F-ac1d with a synthetic parent environment so the planted bug only captures fixture values. F-probe-a through F-probe-f were F-ac2a through F-ac2f in task 002.",
  "retired": {
    "F-ac2a": "Retired: UsersAI binding; AC-002-ARGS. Returns to the falsifiers list once agent_cannot_read_other_agent_memory is live. Mutation remains described in GAPS.md and RUNBOOK.md.",
    "F-ac2b": "Retired: UsersAI binding; AC-002-ARGS. Returns to the falsifiers list once agent_memory_under_own_principal is live. Mutation remains described in GAPS.md and RUNBOOK.md."
  },
